# Rank 1706 / CVE-2021-25900 (GHSA-43w2-9j62-hq99, CWE-787):
# smallvec 0.6's bulk insert planned its allocation from an iterator's size
# hint. `Iterator::size_hint` returns a pair whose first element is only a
# *lower* bound on how many elements the iterator will yield -- the standard
# library documentation is explicit that an iterator may return more than its
# hint, and that the hint "must not be trusted" for anything unsafe -- so
# `reserve(lower_size_bound)` is sound only as long as the code stops writing
# once it reaches that bound. insert_many did not:
#
#   let (lower_size_bound, _) = iter.size_hint();
#   self.reserve(lower_size_bound);
#   unsafe {
#       let mut ptr = self.as_mut_ptr().offset(index as isize);
#       ptr::copy(ptr, ptr.offset(lower_size_bound as isize), old_len - index);
#       self.set_len(index);                       // logical length truncated
#       let mut num_added = 0;
#       for element in iter {                      // driven by the iterator
#           let mut cur = ptr.offset(num_added as isize);
#           if num_added >= lower_size_bound {     // knows it passed the reserve
#               self.reserve(1);                   // grows by one element
#               ptr = self.as_mut_ptr().offset(index as isize);
#               cur = ptr.offset(num_added as isize);
#               ptr::copy(cur, cur.offset(1), old_len - index);
#           }
#           ptr::write(cur, element);
#           num_added += 1;
#       }
#       self.set_len(old_len + num_added);
#   }
#
# `reserve(additional)` sizes the allocation from the collection's *current
# length*, and `set_len(index)` has just cut that length to `index` while
# `ptr::copy` has placed the tail at `lower_size_bound` past it. The in-loop
# `reserve(1)` therefore guarantees capacity for `index + 1` elements while the
# write cursor is at `index + num_added`, so from the second element past the
# bound onward `ptr::write` lands outside the allocation. The advisory's own
# reproducer needs only `size_hint().0 == 0`, which any filter iterator gives.
#
# 5757ac500d4e544485d796b542e4e589749c291b (backport of #254 to the 0.6 branch,
# fixes #253) removes the re-reserve entirely: the unsafe block writes at most
# `lower_size_bound` elements via `while num_added < lower_size_bound`, and any
# surplus is inserted afterwards through the safe per-element
# `self.insert(index + num_added, element)`, which reserves per element from an
# accurate length. The pool row is correct: repository, language, CWE and commit
# all check, the vulnerable construct is present at 7852204 and the remediation
# at 5757ac5. No corpus correction.
#
# Detection is the rust binding rawWritePastSizeHintReservation
# (vyql/bindings/rust/raw_write_past_size_hint_reservation.vyql), reusing
# code.FixedChunkCapacityGrowthIndex and VYQL-MEM-042: a function whose body
# calls size_hint, calls set_len, writes through std::ptr::write, and regrows
# capacity with `self.reserve(<single-digit literal>)`. The regrow-by-literal
# is the defective capacity strategy itself, so a reskin that renames every
# local or inlines the base pointer still matches; the canonical safe form
# (std's Vec::extend_desugared, `self.reserve(lower.saturating_add(1))` from an
# accurate length check) reserves a computed amount and does not.
#
# The literal is matched as body text because every call-argument token route
# flow-expands the call's inputs: `self.reserve(lower.saturating_add(1))` reads
# as though the literal 1 were reserve's own argument, which is why the
# callArg-narrowed form of this binding reports extend_desugared on every
# revision (internal/bindings/bindings_match.go, callArgContextTokensScoped).
# The conjuncts are separate clauses -- size_hint and set_len in one any-of
# list is a disjunction and matches std's own single-element Vec::insert on
# set_len alone.
#
# Measurements (3 x --cache off, timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB): the vulnerable
# checkout reports 23 findings with exactly one VYQL-MEM-042 at lib.rs:825
# (insert_many); the fixed checkout reports 23 findings with none, the delta
# elsewhere being a CFG-014 on the safe per-element insert the fix adds.
# Zero VYQL-MEM-042 across the standard library's own alloc sources (sparse
# checkout of library/alloc/src, and the pinned revisions kept under the
# in-place-collect pair), the rustfs and rust-phonenumber trees, and the
# minimal extend_desugared form below. A grep prefilter for all four
# identifiers in one file over every other Rust tree in the scratch pool
# matches nothing outside the standard library.
#
# Residuals, restated from the binding: prose in a comment can satisfy the
# literal clause (false positive); a computed regrow (`self.reserve(k + 1)`)
# or a multi-digit literal is missed (false negative); and the Rust function
# context carries no ordering fact, so co-membership in one function is the
# strongest available statement of the shape. If the extractor ever emits a
# loop or ordering fact for Rust function contexts, tighten this to require
# the reserve inside the write loop and keep every case below rejected.
#
# The four cases differ only in what bounds the raw write: the iterator
# (vulnerable), the reserved count with a safe fallback (the fixed revision),
# the accurate length (std's correct form, the false positive any literal
# token buys) and a single reserved element (correct one-in-one-out, which a
# bare reserve(1) pairing without the size_hint conjunct buys).
#
# verify_current_expected: fixed, first form expects and the rest reject.

test "rank1706: insert_many writes through a raw pointer past a size-hint reservation, growing capacity one element at a time"
  lang rust
  file lib.rs
  expect VYQL-MEM-042
  expect_review code.FixedChunkCapacityGrowthIndex
  code
  ```
  use std::ptr;

  pub struct SmallVec<T> { data: *mut T, cap: usize, len: usize }

  impl<T> SmallVec<T> {
      pub fn len(&self) -> usize { self.len }
      pub fn as_mut_ptr(&mut self) -> *mut T { self.data }
      pub fn set_len(&mut self, n: usize) { self.len = n }
      pub fn reserve(&mut self, additional: usize) { let _ = additional; }

      pub fn insert_many<I: IntoIterator<Item=T>>(&mut self, index: usize, iterable: I) {
          let iter = iterable.into_iter();
          if index == self.len() {
              return self.extend(iter);
          }

          let (lower_size_bound, _) = iter.size_hint();
          self.reserve(lower_size_bound);

          unsafe {
              let old_len = self.len();
              let mut ptr = self.as_mut_ptr().offset(index as isize);
              ptr::copy(ptr, ptr.offset(lower_size_bound as isize), old_len - index);
              self.set_len(index);

              let mut num_added = 0;
              for element in iter {
                  let mut cur = ptr.offset(num_added as isize);
                  if num_added >= lower_size_bound {
                      self.reserve(1);
                      ptr = self.as_mut_ptr().offset(index as isize);
                      cur = ptr.offset(num_added as isize);
                      ptr::copy(cur, cur.offset(1), old_len - index);
                  }
                  ptr::write(cur, element);
                  num_added += 1;
              }
              self.set_len(old_len + num_added);
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1706: the unsafe write loop bounded by the reserved count, surplus through the safe per-element insert"
  lang rust
  file lib.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-042
  reject_review code.FixedChunkCapacityGrowthIndex
  code
  ```
  use std::ptr;

  pub struct SmallVec<T> { data: *mut T, cap: usize, len: usize }

  impl<T> SmallVec<T> {
      pub fn len(&self) -> usize { self.len }
      pub fn as_mut_ptr(&mut self) -> *mut T { self.data }
      pub fn set_len(&mut self, n: usize) { self.len = n }
      pub fn reserve(&mut self, additional: usize) { let _ = additional; }
      pub fn insert(&mut self, index: usize, element: T) { let _ = (index, element); }

      pub fn insert_many<I: IntoIterator<Item=T>>(&mut self, index: usize, iterable: I) {
          let mut iter = iterable.into_iter();
          if index == self.len() {
              return self.extend(iter);
          }

          let (lower_size_bound, _) = iter.size_hint();
          self.reserve(lower_size_bound);
          let mut num_added = 0;

          unsafe {
              let old_len = self.len();
              let ptr = self.as_mut_ptr().offset(index as isize);
              ptr::copy(ptr, ptr.offset(lower_size_bound as isize), old_len - index);
              self.set_len(index);

              while num_added < lower_size_bound {
                  let element = match iter.next() {
                      Some(x) => x,
                      None => break,
                  };
                  let cur = ptr.offset(num_added as isize);
                  ptr::write(cur, element);
                  num_added += 1;
              }
              self.set_len(old_len + num_added);
          }

          for element in iter {
              self.insert(index + num_added, element);
              num_added += 1;
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1706: a grow-when-full loop that reserves from an accurate length writes raw safely"
  lang rust
  file lib.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-042
  reject_review code.FixedChunkCapacityGrowthIndex
  code
  ```
  use std::ptr;

  pub struct SmallVec<T> { data: *mut T, cap: usize, len: usize }

  impl<T> SmallVec<T> {
      pub fn len(&self) -> usize { self.len }
      pub fn capacity(&self) -> usize { self.cap }
      pub fn as_mut_ptr(&mut self) -> *mut T { self.data }
      pub fn set_len(&mut self, n: usize) { self.len = n }
      pub fn reserve(&mut self, additional: usize) { let _ = additional; }

      pub fn extend_desugared<I: Iterator<Item=T>>(&mut self, mut iterator: I) {
          while let Some(element) = iterator.next() {
              let len = self.len();
              if len == self.capacity() {
                  let (lower, _) = iterator.size_hint();
                  self.reserve(lower.saturating_add(1));
              }
              unsafe {
                  ptr::write(self.as_mut_ptr().add(len), element);
                  self.set_len(len + 1);
              }
          }
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1706: a single-element insert that reserves one and writes one"
  lang rust
  file lib.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-042
  reject_review code.FixedChunkCapacityGrowthIndex
  code
  ```
  use std::ptr;

  pub struct SmallVec<T> { data: *mut T, cap: usize, len: usize }

  impl<T> SmallVec<T> {
      pub fn as_mut_ptr(&mut self) -> *mut T { self.data }
      pub fn reserve(&mut self, additional: usize) { let _ = additional; }
      pub fn set_len(&mut self, n: usize) { self.len = n }

      pub fn insert(&mut self, index: usize, element: T) {
          self.reserve(1);

          unsafe {
              let ptr = self.as_mut_ptr().offset(index as isize);
              ptr::copy(ptr, ptr.offset(1), 0);
              ptr::write(ptr, element);
              self.set_len(index + 1);
          }
      }
  }
  ```
